error[ffi_constant_type]: `PT_OTHER` is `struct other` in `fixedbugs-094-values.h`, not `Pt` — clang read the header and the types disagree
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-094-an-expression-of-another-type-is-told-by-its-type.hero:10:5
     |
  10 |     constant PT_OTHER: Pt  #~ ffi_constant_type
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: an `extern constant` takes its value and its type from the header (§4.19), and is declared at that type or one that holds every value of it — or the header named is not the one that spells `PT_OTHER` as `Pt`

